  "details": "<p>The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: el-Bara</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "el-Bara (also Bara or al-Bara (Arabic: \u0628\u0627\u0631\u0629)) is numbered among one of the so-called \"Dead Cities\" of northwestern Syria. The settlement originates in the fourth century CE and flourishes during the fifth and sixth centuries. It benefited from a favorable position along the route between Antioch and Apamea.",
